{"chunk_id": "acab0d8caf6f", "text": "After Indrajit\u2019s devastating celestial weapon fells Rama, Lakshmana, and vast numbers of the monkey army, despair spreads across the battlefield. Vibhishana reassures the survivors that the princes only submitted to the weapon to honor Brahma\u2019s power. Searching the field at night among mutilated bodies, he and Hanuman find the ancient bear Jambavan badly wounded. Jambavan asks first whether Hanuman lives, declaring that if Hanuman survives, the army is not truly defeated. He instructs Hanuman to fly to the Himalayas and retrieve four luminous healing herbs\u2014Mritasanjivani, Vishalyakarani, Suvarnakarani, and Sandhani. When the herbs hide themselves, Hanuman uproots the entire mountain peak and carries it through the sky back to Lanka. The fragrance revives Rama, Lakshmana, and the fallen monkeys, restoring the army and renewing the war.\nAfter Rama and Lakshmana fall unconscious, Jambavan sends Hanuman to fetch healing herbs from the Himalayas, leading Hanuman to uproot and carry the entire mountain peak.\nThemes: heroic rescue, devotion and duty, healing herbs, divine warfare, Hanuman's power", "vector": [0.0003174868761561811, -0.023300033062696457, -0.008142705075442791, 0.01210124883800745, -0.002832170808687806, 0.0326802097260952, -0.01855524815618992, -0.018268100917339325, -0.01914322003722191, -0.004943052772432566, -0.0003110773104708642, 0.019252609461545944, 0.014617214910686016, 0.00780769856646657, 0.00037431830423884094, -0.0058933766558766365, 0.04739313945174217, -0.021932659670710564, 0.022206135094165802, -0.01776217296719551, -0.001288748811930418, 0.0020271302200853825, -0.012135433964431286, 0.011472257785499096, -0.012525134719908237, 0.012012369930744171, 0.032516125589609146, -0.023190641775727272, 0.01247044000774622, 0.00974253099411726, -0.014480478130280972, -0.014357414096593857, -0.006662523839622736, -0.0030184753704816103, -0.018856070935726166, 0.005384030286222696, -0.0020630236249